```

In this version, I've replaced `-(-sum(well) // capacity)` with `(total_water + capacity - 1) // capacity`, which is a clearer way to perform ceiling division. This ensures that even if the total water in a well is not perfectly divisible by the capacity, the calculation rounds up to ensure all water is emptied.

If the grid does not need to be transposed (i.e., each sublist directly represents a well), you can modify the loop accordingly:

