    [0, 2, 0],
    [1, 0, 3],
    [0, 1, 2]
]
capacity = 3
print(max_fill(grid, capacity))  # Output will depend on the grid and capacity
```

This version uses `(total_water + capacity - 1) // capacity` to round up the division, which is more readable than the original expression. It also includes a docstring to explain what the function does, its parameters, and its return value.
